Kilowatt Country (kilowattcountry)

Inspired by Power Grid.

Game design, rules text, the maps, the power plants, code and art: Luis Montes. The rules are restated in our own
words. The maps are real countries and areas: games/kilowattcountry/tools/gen-maps.mjs picks each map's thirty cities
and links them by its own rules (population and spacing, a Delaunay triangulation cut to its Gabriel edges, five
regions of six grown along the links, each link's cost from the real distance between its cities), and
games/kilowattcountry/tools/make-textures.mjs draws each night map, the table and the glow. The plant set
(games/kilowattcountry/tools/gen-data.mjs) is our own, balance-checked against a worth line. The plant cards are
painted in the game, and the sounds are synthesised in code.

Map data:
- City names, places and populations: GeoNames (geonames.org), licensed under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Extract in games/kilowattcountry/data/places.tsv (towns and cities
  in the maps' countries; names written without accents, a few in their English form, trailing parts such as
  "am Main" cut).
- Land, country borders, lakes, rivers and state lines: Natural Earth (naturalearthdata.com), public domain.

Built with cartwheel-engine and three.c (MIT). The font is the engine's built-in sans (see the engine's NOTICE).
The logo font is Oswald (SIL Open Font Licence, games/kilowattcountry/tools/fonts).
